Could have done better I think. Let me look... I'm learning that
artifacts are good to wish for. You really won't come across them in a game
and they often confer really good effects. For example in my current game
I wished up the Eye of the Aethiopica for my Monk. Not only magic resistance
but I get hungerless manna regen and 1/2 off spell damage.

You may have done well wishing for the Orb of Detection or the Magic
Mirror or Merlin. MR and telepathy for each. 

Another advantage is that since it isn't your artifact, coveteous monsters
like Lichs won't try to steal it from you like they will with your own
quest artifact.

Finally it opens up the cloak slot for a more interesting choice like a
cloak of displacement or a robe.

Not a huge loss, but just something to think about the next time you come
across a wish and you already have your dragon scale (which I normally spend
my first wish on).

> I have an amulet of life saving...

Good. But it's more hand holding if you have poison and magic resistance
and reflection covered. With those three in the bag, instadeaths are greatly
reduced.

