> I'm now at lvl40 but something bad happened at lvl41.
>I was fighting a Lich (which kept teleporting away),

Master Lich. Nasty until you know the trick...

They always teleport to the upstairs of the level. It's their weakness.
One you know it they are much less harmful than before. The upstairs becomes
the high ground. You occupy it and they won't leave. You pound away until
they crumble to dust.

> it summoned master ming flayers which reduced my int down to 4.

They're nasty too. The key to mind flayers is that they have to touch you
do to damage. So you tackle them by jabbing and moving with range weapons.
Magic missile is my favorite. Jumping boots (or the spell) are helpful as they 
allow you to quickly step away from them and blast away.

Not every monster in Nethack requires a physical pounding to get rid of...

Finally you have your quest artifact whose power is level teleport. Presuming
you have teleport control, you could have gotten out of there simply by 
#invoking the Orb of Fate. Come back and fight another day.

